  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Scramble In\n\nText types itself in left to right with a short run of random glyphs ahead of the cursor that resolve into the real letters; several lines can start in a quick cascade.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A list, tracklist or block of text should decode onto the screen line by line with a hacker-style run of random glyphs.\n- You want a fixed-width layout that never reflows while the text appears.\n\nAvoid when:\n- Each word should scramble and lock in on its own: use scramble-reveal or caption-scramble.\n- The text should type with a caret: use typewriter.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"1. Opening Titles - 2:14\\n2. Slow Motion - 3:27\\n3. Night Drive - 4:58\\n4. Paper Planes - 3:45\\n5. Interlude - 1:44\\n6. Golden Hour - 3:57\\n7. Open Road - 3:22\\n8. Something About Us - 3:51\\n9. Last Light - 5:44\\n10. Short Circuit - 3:26\"\n- font_size (number, 12-120): Font size, default 34\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"400\"\n- color (color): Color, default \"#111111\"\n- scrambled_color (color): Scrambled color, default \"#9ca3af\"\n- characters (string): Characters, default \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz!@#$%^&*()_+\"\n- line_height (number, 1-3): Line height, default 1.6\n- scramble_speed (number, 10-200): Scramble speed, default 25\n- scrambled_letters (number, 0-16): Scrambled letters, default 5\n- line_delay (number, 0-1): Line delay, default 0.05\n- start (number, 0-3): Start, default 0.2\n\nSource: https://github.com/danielpetho/fancy. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
